# MultiDaySchedule

**File:** `src/yasched/coring/MultiDaySchedule.py`

A one-off occurrence spanning multiple consecutive calendar days (all-day range,
e.g. a holiday or multi-day conference). No intra-day time is captured.

Inherits from `Schedule`.

---

## YAML form accepted

```yaml
schedule:
  type: multi_day
  start_day: "2026-08-10"
  end_day: "2026-08-14"
```

---

## Fields

| Field       | Type            | Required | Description                     |
|-------------|-----------------|----------|---------------------------------|
| `start_day` | `datetime.date` | yes      | First day (inclusive)           |
| `end_day`   | `datetime.date` | yes      | Last day (inclusive)            |

---

## Interface

```
MultiDaySchedule(Schedule)
  + start_day: datetime.date
  + end_day: datetime.date
```

---

## Invariant

`start_day <= end_day` — enforced by `__post_init__`; raises `ValueError` if
violated. A single-day span (`start_day == end_day`) is allowed; use
`SingleDaySchedule` by convention when the intent is a single day.

---

## Notes

- Frozen dataclass.
- No time components — `MultiDaySchedule` always represents all-day spans.
- Duration is implicitly `(end_day - start_day + 1)` days; `backending`
  computes this when needed.
